From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: handle context faults without an attached domain

SM-T531 ramoops records a boot-time NULL dereference in
report_iommu_fault+0xc, called from qcom_iommu_fault with r0=0.
Context IRQs may arrive before ctx->domain is assigned, including while
firmware scanout is being replaced. report_iommu_fault requires a domain.

Read the domain once and invoke the client callback only when one exists.
Continue logging, acknowledging FSR and terminating the faulting
transaction for unattached contexts, instead of panicking in interrupt
context. This neither bypasses translation nor suppresses the fault.
It does not by itself fix the firmware framebuffer handoff or all
domain-lifetime races.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -223,6 +223,7 @@
 static irqreturn_t qcom_iommu_fault(int irq, void *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_iommu_ctx *ctx = dev;
+	struct iommu_domain *domain;
 	u32 fsr, fsynr;
 	u64 iova;
 
@@ -234,10 +235,13 @@
 	fsynr = iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FSYNR0);
 	iova = iommu_readq(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FAR);
 
-	if (report_iommu_fault(ctx->domain, ctx->dev, iova, 0)) {
+	/* Firmware can leave a pending fault before the first domain attach. */
+	domain = READ_ONCE(ctx->domain);
+	if (!domain || report_iommu_fault(domain, ctx->dev, iova, 0)) {
 		dev_err_ratelimited(ctx->dev,
-				    "Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x%x, "
+				    "%s context fault: fsr=0x%x, "
 				    "iova=0x%016llx, fsynr=0x%x, cb=%d\n",
+				    domain ? "Unhandled" : "Unattached",
 				    fsr, iova, fsynr, ctx->asid);
 	}
 
